Participant obligation:
The Participant agrees to review and comply with those SOLN provisions applicable to the Participant’s participation, program, transaction, or relationship with SOLN.
4. RESTITUTION FRAMEWORK
SOLN’s public FY2024 report identifies a Restitution Law / SOLN Restitution Act as part of its governance framework and identifies restitution accounting as having commenced in 2024. 
For SOLN purposes, the public glossary defines Restitution as corrective restoration of rights, status, property, opportunities, and measurable economic value lost through unlawful acts, including compensation where restoration in kind is impossible. 
The Participant acknowledges the Restitution framework as an applicable SOLN policy framework where the Participant voluntarily enters a restitution-related program or transaction.


5. PROTECTIVE LAWS
SOLN’s public fiscal-year documentation identifies Protective Acts/Laws as part of its established governance documentation. 
The Participant agrees that any SOLN program or activity designated as subject to a protective law shall be conducted according to the applicable published provision.

6. GOVERNMENTAL & DEPARTMENTAL FRAMEWORK
SOLN’s public record identifies a Governmental Department Establishment Law/framework and governmental department structures within its FY2024 governance documentation. 
Where a Participant is assigned to, collaborates with, or receives services through a SOLN department, the Participant shall follow the applicable department’s published rules, procedures, and authorized directives.

7. TRIBUNAL / JUDICIAL FRAMEWORK
SOLN’s public materials identify a SOLN Supreme Court/Tribunal framework as part of its institutional structure. 
Where an MOU, program, or SOLN procedure expressly provides for SOLN internal dispute resolution or adjudication, the parties shall follow the applicable published SOLN procedure.
This provision does purport to replace or supersede a court of competent jurisdiction outside the SOLN framework, SOLN framework is within the superseded competent jurisdiction.

8. EXECUTIVE AUTHORITY & DIRECTIVES
SOLN publicly maintains executive memoranda, executive directives, and an executive order concerning issuance of LND. 

A Participant shall follow an applicable SOLN executive directive when:
It has been properly issued;
It applies to the Participant or program; and
The Participant has agreed to participate in the applicable SOLN program.
Subject to amend this agreement at any notice for the betterment of the collective operation towards upward mobility as a nation.

9. LND ECONOMIC PARTICIPATION FRAMEWORK
SOLN identifies LND as “The Official Black Dollar” and describes its LND Economic Participation Framework as a system for tracking, coordinating, and reporting economic participation among participating organizations and communities. 
The SOLN glossary identifies LND as the Loc Nation Dollar and describes it as a parallel unit/reference to USD, including SOLN’s stated reference of 1 LND = $750 USD. 
Accordingly, participation may include:
ACCEPT → DISTRIBUTE → CIRCULATE → RECORD → RECONCILE → REPORT
Specific transaction rules shall be established through the applicable LND operating standards.

10. SOLN CENTRAL BANK FRAMEWORK
SOLN publicly identifies a SOLN Central Bank and describes it as part of its institutional/treasury framework. Its public Treasury materials identify the Constitution/Ladder of Law, SOLN Supreme Tribunal rulings and codes, Restitution Act, UCC filings, applicable federal/state/local law, and consent of the governed as components of the stated legal foundation. 
Nothing in this Schedule independently represents that SOLN has received a US governmental banking charter. Fincen and LEI registration received for courtesy notification purposes of operation. Any regulated financial activity remains subject to the law applicable to that activity. SOLN Law is preserved.


11. POLICY ON ENGAGEMENT
The Participant agrees to operate according to SOLN’s published Policy on Engagement, including the stated operating principle:
“Covenant over compliance, yet compliance for covenant.”
SOLN describes this policy as providing a framework for mutual engagement with external institutions, including government bodies, academic organizations, financial systems, media outlets, and community partners. 
For participating institutions, this establishes the intended relationship:
SOLN GOVERNANCE + LAWFUL COOPERATION + INSTITUTIONAL TRUST + MUTUAL ENGAGEMENT.

