SOLN JURISDICTION & LND OPERATING FRAMEWORK
The parties acknowledge that the SOLN Constitution, laws, codes, executive instruments, policies, economic instruments, public records, and organizational registrations identified in this Schedule constitute the governing framework established by State of Loc Nation Global Public Benefit Corporation (SOLN GPBC), a sovereign polity for activities conducted within the SOLN jurisdiction.
Within that jurisdiction, SOLN recognizes LND — The Official Black Dollar — as an economic instrument established and administered under the SOLN governing framework for participating persons, businesses, institutions, and communities, particularly those historically affected by redlining, underinvestment, economic exclusion, and lack of representation.
The UCC filings, court records, LEI, LCCN, organizational registrations, and SOLN-issued instruments identified in this Schedule constitute documentary records supporting the establishment, identification, administration, or operation of the SOLN framework and LND activities, according to the legal effect of each respective record.
Nothing in this provision shall be interpreted to alter the legal effect assigned by an external partnering authority to a UCC filing, court record, LEI, LCCN, registration, or other external identifier. The parties’ agreement to participate in the SOLN framework constitutes their voluntary recognition of and commitment to the SOLN rules applicable to their participation.
Where activities involve persons, businesses, institutions, or jurisdictions outside the SOLN jurisdiction, the parties shall establish the applicable relationship through the appropriate agreement, recognition mechanism, or other lawful instrument.
PURPOSE OF LND PARTICIPATION
The parties recognize the SOLN LND framework as an economic-development mechanism intended to connect participating businesses, institutions, and communities; facilitate economic circulation; document economic activity; support business-to-business commerce; and address economic conditions associated with historical redlining, underinvestment, exclusion, and underrepresentation.  SOLN notes are the official paper money used as legal tender in the historical redlining, underinvestment, exclusion, and underrepresentation globally. They serve as a daily medium of exchange for buying goods and paying debts, act as a store of value, and function as the standard SOLN dollar bills ($1, $5, $10, $20, $50, and $100) in circulation upon completion of this agreement. 









